n;c=json.load(open('data/critics.json'))\nprint(c.get('_doc'))\nfor k in c['critics']:\n  if any(w in json.dumps(k).lower() for w in ['phys','sim']): print(json.dumps(k)[:1500])\n\"","description":"Search for sim-related terms and physics critic"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfXzSL5HDhkESJ7BpDHoy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7501072-62e6-410a-a597-f15f93327e5b","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:47:26.386Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
{"parentUuid":"f7501072-62e6-410a-a597-f15f93327e5b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a1f3ebf00c41d2c63","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017QrGPXUApTnHiKyCck3nKF","type":"tool_result","content":"data/capabilities.json:269:        [\"WLD.PART.sim-lod\", \"Simulation LOD & significance management\", \"world-architect\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:277:        [\"WLD.SPACE.index\", \"Generic spatial index & query service for non-physics consumers\", \"spatial-transforms\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:292:        [\"WLD.ENV.buoyancy\", \"Water queries & buoyancy data\", \"water-ocean\", \"E\", [\"character-vehicle-physics\"]],\ndata/capabilities.json:416:        [\"RND.GI.sdf\", \"SDF / voxel scene representations for tracing\", \"global-illumination\", \"E\", [\"ray-tracing-infrastructure\"]]\ndata/capabilities.json:467:        [\"RND.2D.ui-backend\", \"UI render backend (batching, clipping, SDF, HDR compositing)\", \"render-2d-vector\", \"E\", [\"ui-architect\"]],\ndata/capabilities.json:474:        [\"RND.VFX.collision\", \"Particle collision (depth buffer, SDF)\", \"vfx-particles\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:475:        [\"RND.VFX.budgets\", \"VFX budgets, LOD & significance\", \"vfx-particles\", \"E\", [\"performance-architect\"]]\ndata/capabilities.json:489:    {\"id\": \"PHY\", \"name\": \"Physics & simulation\", \"areas\": [\ndata/capabilities.json:553:        [\"ANM.ARCH.sync\", \"Animation / physics / gameplay sync & root-motion policy\", \"animation-architect\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:696:        [\"NET.PRED.physics\", \"Networked physics\", \"prediction-rollback\", \"E\", [\"rigid-body-dynamics\"]],\ndata/capabilities.json:774:        [\"UI.TXT.raster\", \"Glyph rasterization (SDF, MSDF, GPU curves)\", \"text-fonts\", \"E\"],\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:9:1. **Distinct expertise.** It needs a body of knowledge (literature, APIs, hardware behavior) that a neighboring skill does not need. For example, a tire model and a solver share a physics lead but not a literature.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:38:- **Cycles.** Runtime data does flow both ways. Animation feeds physics (kinematic bodies) and physics feeds animation (ragdoll, foot IK). Those flows go through frame phases declared in `C-FRAME`, never through direct calls. Required-edge cycles between skills are listed in `02-skill-dependency-graph.md` so each gets an explicit phase-mediated design.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:48:- **End-to-end feature ownership.** An environment feature (terrain, water, vegetation, atmosphere) is owned end to end by one skill: representation, simulation, rendering and tool logic. It consumes render, physics and editor contracts. The alternative, splitting terrain rendering from terrain data from terrain tools, creates three agents who must change in lock-step for every terrain feature.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:85:| `render-2d-vector` is also the UI and debug-overlay draw backend. | Sprite batching, SDF text and vector paths share one technique set. Without this, three 2D renderers would be built. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:91:| `physics-2d` is separate from 3D dynamics. | 2D engines (Box2D class) use different data layouts and solvers. The 2D configuration must not carry the 3D engine. |\nCritic framework. scope selectors: 'all', 'tier:<tier>', 'subtree:<skill-id>' (the skill and all descendants), or a bare skill id. Stages: G1 = framework gauntlet (this phase; every critic reviews the whole framework), G2 = SKILL.md gauntlet (per-skill, scoped), S1 = ADR review, S2 = design/contract review, S3 = implementation review, S4 = validation & release review.\n{\"id\": \"K-SIM\", \"name\": \"Physics & Simulation Critic\", \"mandate\": \"Simulation domains: physics, destruction, fluids, cloth, crowds, large-scale simulation, determinism of simulation.\", \"checks\": [\"stepping and sync with frame phases are explicit\", \"determinism levels are declared\", \"simulation LOD exists for large scales\", \"build-vs-integrate evidence\"], \"scope\": [\"subtree:physics-architect\", \"crowd-simulation\", \"ik-procedural-animation\", \"prediction-rollback\", \"determinism-replay\", \"procedural-generation\", \"water-ocean\", \"vfx-particles\"], \"stages\": [\"G1\", \"G2\", \"S1\", \"S2\", \"S3\", \"S4\"]}\n{\"id\": \"K-GAMEPLAY\", \"name\": \"Game Systems & Content Critic\", \"mandate\": \"Animation, audio, AI, gameplay framework, UI, text, localization and accessibility: whether game teams get what they need.\", \"checks\": [\"designers and animators have authoring paths\", \"accessibility and localization built in, not bolted on\", \"gameplay extension points\"], \"scope\": [\"subtree:animation-architect\", \"subtree:audio-architect\", \"subtree:gameplay-architect\", \"subtree:ui-architect\", \"accessibility\", \"input-system\", \"input-devices-haptics\", \"character-vehicle-physics\"], \"stages\": [\"G1\", \"G2\", \"S1\", \"S2\", \"S4\"]}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cd08d2a9-b9c3-4ff3-90ad-403194a25925","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:47:26.466Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f7501072-62e6-410a-a597-f15f93327e5b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
